  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Showers and perhaps a brief thunderstorm tapering \noff from northwest to southeast early today. \n\nA cold front nearly bisecting PA from NE to SW will push slowly\nsouth through the rest of the state this afternoon and evening \nbefore stalling out just south of the Mason/Dixon line today.\nMain factor favoring showers early on is the dewpoints across\nthe far southeast are still quite high.\n\nMuch of the rain so far is not reaching the ground. Widespread\nmid level cloud deck over the area. There is a heavier shower\n(small thing) over Somerset Co.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: A nice afternoon today, but increasing chance \nfor widespread moderate to perhaps heavy rain late Saturday into\nearly Sunday. \n\nStill a bit early to tell how much the models may suffer a\nbit of convective feedback, but the current pattern supports\nwhat we have been having for much of the summer.\n\nMore information below.\n\nAs SFC high pressure moves well off the Mid Atlantic and \nSouthern New England Coast, low level moisture lurking just \nsouth of the Mason/Dixon line Fri night will push steadily NE \nacross the state on Saturday within broad llvl flow from the \nsouth to southwest. A notable axis of streamline convergence \nshifting gradually east across Central PA late Sat afternoon/Sat\nnight will provide increasing llvl theta-E advection and \nnumerous showers with a few to several tenths of an inch of \nrainfall likely across at least the SE half to two thirds of \nthe CWA by early Sunday. A few PM TSRA possible Saturday and/or \nSunday afternoons, especially over the western mtns. A more- \nactive (wetter) pattern is in store for Mon-Tues. But, the flat \nupper ridge over the southern half of the CONUS will make it \ndifficult for deep moisture to make it into PA ahead of any \nshots of atmos forcing. The week could end dry as the upper \nridge pumps up over the central CONUS.",
